From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:40:05 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_ppe: clear only the expired L2 subflow

When one subflow of a bridged flow expires (its slot leaves BIND),
the stats update clears the whole L2 flow instead of that subflow.
The clear frees every subflow while the loop still holds the next
one, and it takes the L2 flow out of the table that new subflows
attach to.

Only the expired subflow goes away now. The L2 flow keeps its other
subflows and can take new ones.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.c
@@ -719,7 +719,7 @@ mtk_flow_entry_update_l2(struct mtk_ppe
 		if (!mtk_flow_entry_update(ppe, cur, packets, bytes)) {
 			entry->prev_packets += cur->prev_packets;
 			entry->prev_bytes += cur->prev_bytes;
-			__mtk_foe_entry_clear(ppe, entry, false);
+			__mtk_foe_entry_clear(ppe, cur, false);
 			continue;
 		}
 
